============================================================================================
LRC14 1260/2520 TOTIENT READOUT
============================================================================================
THM-523 half-clash = 1/2520; denominator = 2520=2^3*3^2*5*7
symmetry doubles to 1/1260; denominator = 1260=2^2*3^2*5*7

Totient-copy resonance:
  phi(14)   = 6   -> unit seam size (Z/14Z)^* and F_7^*
  phi(210)  = 48  -> full squarefree mod-210 exact-period copies
  phi(1260) = 288 -> exact-period copies at raw K14 product
  phi(2520) = 576 -> exact-period copies at half-clash denominator
  full-mask mass of q=1260 = 576, equal to phi(2520).

Denominators in the half-clash, with exact-period copy densities:
  q=  36=     2^2*3^2: phi=  12, phi/q=1/3, rad=6
  q=   5=           5: phi=   4, phi/q=4/5, rad=5
  q=  70=       2*5*7: phi=  24, phi/q=12/35, rad=70
  q= 504=   2^3*3^2*7: phi= 144, phi/q=2/7, rad=42
  q=2520= 2^3*3^2*5*7: phi= 576, phi/q=8/35, rad=210
  q=1260= 2^2*3^2*5*7: phi= 288, phi/q=8/35, rad=210

Readout: the dyadic doubling from 1260 to 2520 is not cosmetic.  It turns the exact-period unit count into 576, the same mass obtained by selecting all four prime masks inside the raw 1260 profile.  That is the arithmetic shadow of the half-gap before tau<->1-tau symmetry halves the denominator.

